.entire/snapshots/GENESIS_FLOW-2026-02-13T17-00-50Z-29d980e.json:24:    "A5": "[A5 RESPONSE]\n\n**Stage 1 iOS Scaffold - 2 Week MVP**\n\n**Core Components:**\n1. **HealthKit Reader** - Request HRV, sleep, step permissions only. Read-only wrapper.\n2. **Simple State Store** - ObservableObject holding current x_t vector (6 floats)\n3. **Main Dashboard** - Single view showing current state as basic gauges/bars\n4. **Manual Input Sheet** - Sliders for mood/energy/cognitive load when HealthKit gaps exist\n5. **Basic Persistence** - Core Data entity storing daily snapshots\n\n**SwiftUI Str",
.entire/snapshots/GENESIS_FLOW-2026-02-13T17-00-50Z-29d980e.json:25:    "A6": "[A6 RESPONSE]\n\n**Current State Assessment:**\n- `.env` key wiring: Critical blocker. Need API keys for OpenAI/Anthropic models properly loaded\n- Async implementation: Half-done, causing bottlenecks in multi-agent coordination\n- Semantic similarity: Stub functions present, needs vector embedding integration\n- Retry logic: Missing entirely, will fail on API rate limits\n\n**Fastest Path to First Live Tribunal:**\n1. **Immediate (2-4 hours):** Fix `.env` loading with python-dotenv, hardcode basic retry",
.entire/snapshots/GENESIS_FLOW-2026-02-13T17-00-50Z-29d980e.json:26:    "A7": "[A7 RESPONSE]\n\n**TestFlight → AppStore Timeline (8-12 weeks)**\n\nWeek 1-2: Core iOS MVP (bridge parity only)\nWeek 3-4: Internal TestFlight with 5-10 power users\nWeek 5-8: External TestFlight (100 users), iterate on onboarding\nWeek 9-12: App Store submission + review cycle\n\n**Free Tier Design (Hunter-Gatherer Calibrated)**\n\nCore free features:\n- Basic bridge creation (1 active bridge)\n- 7-day habit tracking window\n- Simple progress visualization\n- Community sharing (read-only)\n\nPremium unlock trig",
.entire/snapshots/GENESIS_FLOW-2026-02-13T17-00-50Z-29d980e.json:27:    "A8": "[A8 RESPONSE]\n\nUpon reviewing the GENESIS_INIT snapshot and the responses from all agents, my analysis is as follows:\n\n1. **Logical Gaps:**\n   - The state vector \\( x_t \\) lacks explicit representation of social interactions and environmental context, which are critical for episodic memory and may influence other variables like mood (M_t) and energy (E_t).\n   - There's an absence of feedback mechanisms to adjust the state vector based on historical data and outcomes, which is essential for refin"
